  "verbalization": "Bleomycin, a DNA-damaging agent, is implicated in the pathogenesis of Non-hodgkin Lymphoma through a multi-step mechanism involving the induction of cell cycle arrest and apoptosis. The evidence suggests that Bleomycin may act as a bridge in the treatment of Non-hodgkin Lymphoma via its interaction with Vinblastine, which in turn targets Non-hodgkin Lymphoma cells. This pathway is supported by the indication of Bleomycin in B-cell Neoplasm and Langerhans Cell Histiocytosis, both of which are associated with Non-hodgkin Lymphoma. The shared mode of action—DNA damage and subsequent cell death—underpins the potential for Bleomycin to contribute to the treatment of this malignancy. The integration of these pathways highlights the role of Bleomycin in the broader context of chemotherapy for Non-hodgkin Lymphoma, though further mechanistic validation is required to confirm its direct therapeutic effect.",
